update public.outfits set title = $t$Urban layers$t$, explanation = $t$Layering is ideal for Mexico City's weather; the t-shirt adds a subtle touch of color under the open black sweatshirt. The blue pants balance the visual weight of the top, for an urban, functional and very comfortable style.

Let the bottom hem of the t-shirt peek out under the sweatshirt to create visual depth.$t$, weather = $j${"ciudad": "Mexico City", "descripcion": "cloudy", "temperatura": 16}$j$::jsonb where id = '27b9a140-34b4-4fe9-a127-62bdd9aecf10';
update public.outfits set title = $t$Urban romantic$t$, explanation = $t$A great way to wear your red dress in cool weather is with the black sweatshirt on top, which visually turns it into a flared skirt. The contrast of vibrant red with black neutralizes the sporty side of the look, giving you an original, warm option.

Pair it with black track-sole boots to reinforce the urban aesthetic and protect you from the cold.$t$, weather = $j${"ciudad": "Mexico City", "descripcion": "cloudy", "temperatura": 16}$j$::jsonb where id = '475ff9c6-d556-4707-8bfc-c89c9f5f4a49';
update public.outfits set title = $t$Relaxed streetwear$t$, explanation = $t$The grey and brown sweatshirt will give you just the right warmth for 19 degrees and the city's drizzle. With the blue pants, you get a very comfortable casual balance, ready for any errand of the day.

